      <!-- ============ SKETCH 4: WHEEL ANATOMY ============ -->
      <section class="block container narrow" data-notes="The insight, named. &quot;The wheel sits in the lower corner, inside the natural zone, where the holding thumb comes to rest. Spin it for depth and gain — high-frequency actions live on the arc. Deliberate actions get a deliberate gesture: press-and-hold, so a slip in slick gloves never discards patient data. A fixed Home stays in thumb reach — a panic button when the field gets loud. And the dashed ring is the part you never see: the hitbox is bigger than the wheel, on purpose, for a gloved thumb.&quot; Then the field detail: &quot;And it works landscape or portrait — the wheel lives at whichever corner the thumb lands on. However the device comes out of the pocket, you start. Seconds matter in the field; nobody gets to rotate a screen first.&quot;">
        <h2 class="display-h hollow sec-h" data-reveal>The radial thumb-wheel.</h2>
        <p class="lede" data-reveal>The wheel sits in the lower corner — inside the natural zone — right where the holding thumb comes to rest. You spin it, or slide it out with a small sweep, to change depth or gain without breaking concentration or shifting your grip. High-frequency actions live on the arc. Deliberate actions get a deliberate gesture: press-and-hold, so a slip in slick gloves never discards patient data. And a large, fixed Home stays anchored in thumb reach — a panic button that resets you to the live scan when the field gets loud.</p>
        <p class="lede"><strong>Landscape or portrait — it doesn't matter.</strong> The wheel lives at whichever corner the holding thumb lands on, so however the device comes out of a pocket, you start using it. Seconds matter in the field; nobody gets to rotate a screen first.</p>
        <figure class="sketch" data-reveal>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 900 460" role="img" aria-label="Hand sketch of the wheel anatomy: a radial wheel in the lower thumb zone with callouts for spin to adjust depth and gain, press-and-hold for mode, a fixed home button, and an oversized invisible hitbox for a gloved thumb.">
