      <section class="block container narrow" data-notes="The thesis close for this act. &quot;Thirteen years later I'm building an interface you drive with your gaze, your voice and your hands — and the cursor at the center of it is a radial HUD. That isn't a coincidence. Same insight: put the control on a radius matched to a motion the body already makes. In 2013 the motion was a thumb pivoting while the other hand held a probe. In 2026 it's an eye settling on a target. Design for the hand you have free — or the body you actually have — and the paradigm takes care of the rest.&quot; Then the segue: accessibility always enters the picture." data-stage-cs="resolution">
